FONT: Setup_Font/Duplicate_Font contiguous 0x18-byte sprite descriptor (scattered-locals)

Setup_Sprite fills a 0x18-byte sprite descriptor through its 3rd arg; Ghidra split the
stack buffer into short[6] + four loose tail fields (Setup_Font: local_1c/local_10/
uStack_e/local_a/local_9; Duplicate_Font: local_30/local_24/uStack_22/local_1e/local_1d)
-- the 12-byte array under-sizes the write (OOB smash) and the tail reads are
layout-dependent. The prior dd2.exe-era patch (old 090) neither enlarged the buffer nor
survived re-typing: its `local_1c + 0xc` reads were SHORT-scaled (=+24 bytes, garbage).
Both functions now use one undefined1[0x18] with byte-exact tail reads (+0xc,+0xe,
+0x12,+0x13 per the original frame offsets). This is the font/HUD sprite-init path whose
failure left the static loading/HUD prims (e.g. @0x931d88) all-zero -> degenerate spans
oversprayed the BSS (watchpoint-proven self-corruption, L1 frontier).

